From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VyOS LS1046A CI <ci@vyos-ls1046a>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 03:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman_pcd: fe_flow debugfs show full key (fix 8-byte truncation)

The fe_flow debugfs read handler was hardcoded to display the first 16
bytes of the DDR flow record, which includes the 8-byte bucket pointer
(old_native) plus the first 8 bytes of the flow key. For 13-byte 5-tuple
keys (SIP+DIP+PROTO+SPORT+DPORT), this truncated the last 5 bytes,
making it impossible to verify TCP/UDP flow matching.

Fix: display only the flow key portion starting at FMAN_EHASH_FLOW_KEY_OFF
(offset 8) for flow->key_size bytes, skipping the bucket pointer prefix.

Record layout (from fman_pcd_ehash_add_key):
  [0-7]   = old_native (bucket head pointer, swab64)
  [8+]    = flow key (key_size bytes)
  [8+key_size aligned] = next-FE pointer (ENQ FE MURAM offset)

Before: displayed bytes 0-15 (bucket ptr + first 8 key bytes)
After:  displays bytes 8 to 8+key_size-1 (full key only)

Verified: 13-byte key 0A63026A0A6302B906AD9CD903 now displays in full
instead of truncated to 0A63026A0A6302B9 (SIP+DIP only).
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
@@ -261,11 +261,12 @@ static int fman_pcd_fe_flow_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
+		unsigned int n = 0;
+
+		list_for_each_entry(flow, &t->flows, node) {
+			u64 rec_phys = (u64)virt_to_phys(flow->record);
+			const u8 *r = flow->record;
++			const u8 *key = r + FMAN_EHASH_FLOW_KEY_OFF;
+			unsigned int i;
+
+			seq_printf(s,
+				   "tbl[%u] flow[%u] bucket=0x%04x rec=0x%llx ",
+				   ti, n++, flow->index,
+				   (unsigned long long)rec_phys);
+-			for (i = 0; i < 16; i++)
+-				seq_printf(s, "%02x", r[i]);
++			for (i = 0; i < flow->key_size; i++)
++				seq_printf(s, "%02x", key[i]);
+			seq_puts(s, "\n");
+			total++;
+		}
